{number: 144}
{title: Singing I Go}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
The [Ab] trusting heart to Jesus clings,
Nor any [Db] ill can [Ab] fear;
Safe sheltered 'neath His loving wings,
And feeling [Eb7] He is [Ab] near.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Ab] Singing I go along life's road,
Praising the [Db] Lord, praising the [Ab] Lord;
Singing I go along life's road,
For [Eb7] Jesus has lifted my [Ab] load.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
The [Ab] passing cloud may bring its shade,
The [Db] tempest blow a-[Ab] pace;
My trusting soul is not afraid,
Upheld by [Eb7] His dear [Ab] grace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
He [Ab] gives me peace, He gives me song,
His [Db] joy is full and [Ab] free;
My steps are glad the whole day long,
Since [Eb7] Jesus walks with [Ab] me.
{end_of_verse}
